**Neovim is using `cargo check`, which doesn’t run Clippy’s lints.** I checked your running session: zero diagnostics, while your latest cached Clippy run contains **419 errors**.

There are two configuration issues:

1. Your [Rust settings](/Users/jamie/.config/nvim/lua/custom/plugins/lsp/lspconfig.lua:204) never set `check.command = 'clippy'`. Rust-analyzer defaults to `check`. [Docs](https://rust-analyzer.github.io/book/configuration#rust-analyzer.check.command)

2. Your [LSP setup](/Users/jamie/.config/nvim/lua/custom/plugins/lsp/lspconfig.lua:235) uses Mason’s old `handlers` option. Your installed version removed that option, so your custom server settings aren’t being applied. I confirmed they’re absent from the running client. [Migration notes](https://github.com/mason-org/mason-lspconfig.nvim/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#200-2025-05-06)

To enable Clippy, add this **before** `require('mason-lspconfig').setup`:

```lua
vim.lsp.config('rust_analyzer', {
  settings = {
    ['rust-analyzer'] = {
      check = { command = 'clippy' },
    },
  },
})
```

Restart Neovim and save a Rust file.

Your [crate attributes](/Users/jamie/development/exposed/exposed/src/lib/lib.rs:1) turn several Clippy lint groups into errors. Those attributes control Clippy’s severity; they don’t make `cargo check` run Clippy.

No files changed.

